---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { EMAIL, SITE_NAME_FULL, ADDRESS_LOCALITY, ADDRESS_REGION } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Modern Slavery Statement | A2 Commercial Fit Out"
  description="A2 Commercial Fit Out's statement on preventing modern slavery and human trafficking in our business and supply chain."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Modern Slavery Statement' }]} />
  </div>

  <section class="section--tight bg-white">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Modern slavery statement</h1>
      <p>{SITE_NAME_FULL} is committed to preventing modern slavery and human trafficking in our business and supply chain. The formal reporting duty under section 54 of the Modern Slavery Act 2015 applies to organisations above a specified annual turnover threshold, which we do not currently meet — but we're publishing this statement voluntarily because we think transparency on this issue shouldn't depend on company size.</p>

      <h2>Our business</h2>
      <p>{SITE_NAME_FULL} is a fixed-price commercial fit out contractor based in {ADDRESS_LOCALITY}, {ADDRESS_REGION}, delivering office, retail, healthcare and related fit out and refurbishment projects across London, Kent, Essex and the wider South East.</p>

      <h2>Our supply chain</h2>
      <p>Our core trades — dry lining, suspended ceilings, tape & jointing and tiling — are delivered by our own in-house tradespeople rather than subcontracted out, which gives us direct oversight of who is working on our sites. Where we do engage specialist subcontractors and suppliers, such as for M&E installation, we work with a small, established network of partners rather than a large, constantly changing supply base.</p>

      <h2>Our commitments</h2>
      <p>We do not tolerate slavery, servitude, forced or compulsory labour, or human trafficking in any part of our business or supply chain. We expect every subcontractor and supplier we work with to treat the people carrying out their work fairly, lawfully and with dignity, and to hold appropriate right-to-work documentation for anyone on our sites.</p>
      <p>We hold CHAS and SafeContractor accreditation, which includes independent verification of our health and safety and compliance management, and we deliver every project in line with CDM 2015 and current Building Regulations.</p>

      <h2>Due diligence</h2>
      <p>Before engaging a new subcontractor or supplier, we check their trading history, accreditation and, where relevant, their own health and safety and compliance standards. Right-to-work checks are carried out for everyone working on our sites, and we expect the same standard from any subcontractor supplying their own labour. If we ever had reason to believe modern slavery was taking place within our business or supply chain, we would investigate immediately and end the relationship with any party found to be responsible.</p>

      <h2>Raising a concern</h2>
      <p>If you have any concern about modern slavery or human trafficking connected to our business or supply chain, please contact us at <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. All concerns will be treated seriously and in confidence.</p>

      <h2>Keeping this statement up to date</h2>
      <p>This statement reflects the size and structure of our business today. As A2 Commercial Fit Out grows, we expect to formalise additional governance, supplier due diligence and training processes, and we'll update this page to reflect that as it happens.</p>
      <p class="statement-date">Last updated: July 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .statement-date {
    color: var(--text-on-light-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
